  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-IP24-UGA177</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved protection at work and more robust and resilient social and solidarity economy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Uganda, the ILO is supporting the Government, constituents and national partners, in addressing key gaps in social protection, labor migration frameworks, and labor rights to ensure the inclusion and empowerment of vulnerable groups, including informal economy workers, migrant workers, refugees, and host communities. The support focuses on promoting fair and effective labor institutions and services while fostering safe and healthy working environments and equitable access to social protection. This initiative aims to expand social security coverage and enhance policies to be inclusive, gender-responsive, and sustainable. It includes building the capacity of government institutions, social partners, and civil society to develop and implement inclusive social protection strategies. The program also supports efforts to improve labor migration frameworks, negotiate bilateral labor agreements, and raise awareness of labor rights among workers, particularly migrant workers and refugees. Aligned with Uganda&#x2019;s National Development Plan III and international labor standards, the strategy emphasizes collaboration with key stakeholders such as the Ministry of Gender, Labour and Social Development, the National Social Security Fund, and private sector players. Expected outcomes include enhanced governance and financing of social protection systems, expanded access to social security for vulnerable populations, and improved conditions for migrant workers. By fostering inclusive development, this initiative contributes to Uganda&#x2019;s socio-economic resilience and progress toward Sustainable Development Goals 1 (No Poverty), 8 (Decent Work and Economic Growth), and 10 (Reduced Inequalities)</narrative>
  </description>
